  "query_preview": ".. High pressure remains in place across the Four \nCorners with UT settled well within a southwest flow regime serving \nto push monsoonal moisture across the area. Currently, widely \nscattered showers and thunderstorms are ongoing and forecast to \nincrease in coverage throughout the afternoon into the evening. \nPWATs in excess of 1\" will overspread much of UT with southwest UT \npotentially seeing PWAT's in excess of 1.3\" per mesoanalysis. This \nwill enable mature storms to produce heavy rainfall this afternoon, \npotentially yielding a flash flooding threat for slow-moving storms, \nespecially those over problematic terrain. \n\nAs the ridge progresses east somewhat tomorrow afternoon, this will \nallow a trough over the PNW to deepen somewhat resulting in stronger \nforcing over the area tomorrow afternoon into Friday afternoon. \nFriday remains somewhat uncertain regarding the flooding threat \ngiven moisture quality is up in the air, though tomorrow looks to \nmaintain robust moisture across much of the state potentially \nenhancing the flooding threat. Additionally, stronger ascent via the \naforementioned trough may potentially yield more widespread mature \nstorms, increasing the flash flood risk on a larger scale. One \nfailure mode with tomorrow regarding flash flooding will be faster \nstorm motions, though training storms remains possible tomorrow \nafternoon which may offset this. \n\nCome Saturday and Sunday, low-level moisture will decrease following \nthe passage of a cold front. Mid-upper moisture remains in place, \nhowever, resulting in daily afternoon thunderstorms persisting \nacross higher terrain across much of UT in the afternoon hours. \nAdditionally, this will serve to lower afternoon temperatures to \nroughly 10F below average across much of the state. \n\nOn Monday, the ridge looks to retrogress west centering itself over \nthe Four Corners region once again, opening up UT to more monsoonal \nmoisture return. As of now, chances appear rather favorable for the \nmonsoonal moisture pattern to continue through much of next week, \nbringing daily chances for showers and thunderstorms to much of UT \nonce again. Additionally, temperatures look to remain moderated \nfollowing a brief warm-up into Monday with seasonally normal \ntemperatures persisting through at least Wednesday.",
